  "output": {
    "answer": "It did ship, but not on the strength of that one 201-photo test. I flagged it precisely because it was found after my favorite idea failed the bar, on the same photos — that's a coincidence I wanted checked, not trusted outright. It went out behind a flag rather than as a plain announced win, and it was flipped into production only after a replay reproduced the first-guess numbers. The training itself was held out separately: the language head trained on catalogue images only with its one knob set on a separate dev split, and none of the 201 test photos touched that training.",
